# Quina, Qu Gourmet and Doubling Season both replace Bot1's token creations; Bot1 chooses which applies first (CR 616.1),
# and Quina's Frog is part of the event, so Doubling Season doubles it if it applies after (CR 616.1f), and Quina applies
# once to the event, however many kinds of token it makes (CR 614.5).
# - Turn 5: Frontline Rush makes two Goblins. Doubling Season first: four Goblins, then one Frog.
# - Turn 7: Reckoner Bankbuster's last charge counter makes a Treasure and a Pilot together. Quina first: a Treasure, a
#   Pilot and one Frog, all doubled: two of each.
# - Then "{2}, Sacrifice a Frog: Put a +1/+1 counter on Quina": a Goblin and Bot2's Halo Hopper (a Frog) are refused, a
#   Frog token is sacrificed, exactly {2} is paid, and its one counter is doubled to two.

